## Mandatory conventions

> All code in this repository MUST follow
> [docs/agents/coding_guidelines.md](docs/agents/coding_guidelines.md).
> Read it before the first edit. It is hand-written and never regenerated:
> `/ai-context` does not own it and never overwrites it.

### Never in this repository

- A write outside a model method. `create()`, `update()`, `save()`, `delete()`,
  `increment()`, `attach()` and `sync()` never appear in an Action — the Action
  orders the write, the model performs it.
- A second public method on an Action, or `static` anywhere on one. `handle()` is
  the only public method, always called on an injected instance.
- A policy, gate or validator below the entry point. No `Gate::`, `authorize()`,
  `can()`, `auth()`, `request()`, `Validator::`, `validate()` or `Rule::` in
  `app/Actions/`, `app/Models/`, `app/Jobs/`, `app/Listeners/` or `app/Gateways/`.
- `abort()` or an `HttpException` below the entry point. Domain failures are typed
  exceptions carrying a `DomainErrorKind`; `bootstrap/app.php` maps kind to status.
- A bare `where()` in an Action. Every predicate is a `#[Scope]`; raw SQL appears
  only for aggregates inside a report Action.
- An array crossing a class boundary. Public arguments and returns are models, VOs,
  DTOs, enums or typed Collections.
- A `*Service`, `*Manager` or `*Repository` class. One Action per intent.

